Summary
Implement Migration Reconciliation and Migration Completion
Description
Overview
Implement reconciliation to verify that the migration completed successfully before applying final constraints and resuming BAU.
The reconciliation should provide sufficient evidence that all expected records were migrated correctly.
Reconciliation Checks
At minimum:
CSV Record Count
        =
Expected Migration Record Count

        ↓

MAIN Migrated Record Count
        =
Expected Count

        ↓

Audit Record Count
        =
Migrated Record Count

        ↓

Outbox Event Count
        =
Migrated Record Count

        ↓

Failed Records
        =
0
Additional checks should include:
Records from the CSV exist in MAIN.
All applicable fields contain expected migrated values.
Mandatory migration fields are populated.
Target data version is correct.
No unexpected records were modified.
Audit entries exist for migrated records.
Outbox events exist for migrated records.
Implementation Methods
generateReconciliationReport();

validateMigrationResult();

completeMigration();
If you want to keep it simpler, these can be:
reconcileMigration();

completeMigration();
Completion Flow
Migration
    ↓
Reconciliation
    ↓
All Checks Pass?
   /       \
 No         Yes
 ↓           ↓
FAILED    Apply Constraints
             ↓
